## Why This Is Asked

Tests DP formulation for selecting fixed-count non-overlapping subarrays with a per-block cost, plus reconstruction of blocks.

## Key Concepts

- DP over i (prefix) and t (blocks)
- Prefix sums for subarray sums
- Running best to avoid O(n^2)
- Reconstructing start/end indices

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxKSubarraysWithCost(A, k, c){
  const n = A.length;
  const pref = new Array(n+1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n; i++) pref[i+1] = pref[i] + A[i];
  const NEG = -1e15;
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(NEG));
  const from = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(null));
  dp[0][0] = 0;
  const bestVal = new Array(k+1).fill(NEG);
  const bestIdx = new Array(k+1).fill(-1);
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++){
    for (let t = 0; t <= k; t++){
      dp[i][t] = dp[i-1][t];
      from[i][t] = {type:'skip', at:i-1, t};
    }
    for (let t = 1; t <= k; t++){
      const val = dp[i-1][t-1] - pref[i-1];
      if (val > bestVal[t]) { bestVal[t] = val; bestIdx[t] = i-1; }
      const cand = bestVal[t] + pref[i] - c;
      if (cand > dp[i][t]) {
        dp[i][t] = cand;
        from[i][t] = {type:'end', end:i-1, start:bestIdx[t], t};
      }
    }
  }
  let i = n, t = k;
  const blocks = [];
  while (i > 0 && t > 0){
    const info = from[i][t];
    if (!info) break;
    if (info.type === 'end'){
      blocks.push([info.start, info.end]);
      i = info.start;
      t--;
    } else {
      i = info.at;
    }
  }
  blocks.reverse();
  return { value: dp[n][k], blocks };
}
```

## Follow-up Questions

- How would you adapt for at-most-k blocks?
- How would you handle negative values of c or allow zero-cost blocks?
- What modifications optimize space to O(k) while preserving reconstruction?

## Why This Is Asked

Tests ability to design a DP with partitioning and additive segment costs; uses prefix sums to optimize the transition to O(nk).

## Key Concepts

- DP on partitioning into k segments
- Prefix sums to compute segment costs in O(1)
- State transition optimization with a running max and backpointers
- Reconstruction of cut points

## Code Example

```javascript
function maxPartitionScore(A, k){
  const n = A.length;
  if (k <= 0 || k > n) return {score: 0, cuts: []};
  const diff = new Array(n-1).fill(0);
  for (let i = 0; i < n-1; i++) diff[i] = Math.abs(A[i+1] - A[i]);
  const pref = new Array(n).fill(0);
  for (let i = 1; i < n; i++) pref[i] = pref[i-1] + diff[i-1];
  const dp = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-Infinity));
  const take = Array.from({length: n+1}, () => new Array(k+1).fill(-1));
  for (let i = 1; i <= n; i++) dp[i][1] = pref[i-1];
  for (let t = 2; t <= k; t++) {
    let best = -Infinity, bestP = -1;
    for (let i = t; i <= n; i++) {
      const p = i - 1;
      const val = dp[p][t-1] - pref[p];
      if (val > best) { best = val; bestP = p; }
      dp[i][t] = pref[i-1] + best;
      take[i][t] = bestP;
    }
  }
  let cuts = [];
  let i = n, t = k;
  while (t > 0) {
    const p = take[i][t];
    cuts.push(i);
    i = p;
    t--;
  }
  cuts.reverse();
  return {score: dp[n][k], cuts};
}
```

